                <pb facs="1012" n="908" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg908"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.1051/723: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-16T12:00:00-05:45">December 16,
                            1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 10:33 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>239. My 232 December 7, 3 p.m. All grades in the Guardia have now been filled
                    with Nicaraguan officers who are at their posts. In accordance with the
                    pre-electoral agreement between the political parties to continue the Guardia
                    Nacional as a nonpartisan, noncombatant institution, one half of the officers in
                    each grade newly appointed to the higher grades are Liberals and one half
                    Conservatives. All American officers were withdrawn yesterday from the
                    departments of Nueva Segovia, Jinotega, Esteli, Matagalpa, and Chontales and all
                    posts in those departments are now commanded by Nicaraguan officers under
                    control of course of the headquarters in Managua. Complete evacuation of all
                    American troops from Nicaragua will be effected January 2.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
